        <text x="320" y="36" font-family="EB Garamond, serif" font-size="12" fill="#ffd979" text-anchor="middle" font-style="italic">one route, drawn: up to ten, then the fork</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <p class="plate-note">The same spiral and the same numbering as Plate&nbsp;I, with a single journey laid
      over it. The gold road climbs the first decade one station at a time. At ten it splices: the faint
      green road is the half that carries on outward into the next density, and the rose road is the half
      sent back &mdash; which does not re-enter at one and start again, but passes <em>below</em> it. Each
      further fall is shorter than the last by the golden ratio, so the stations crowd toward the ground
      without ever reaching it. Nought stays untrodden, and the crowd at the bottom of everything is built
      out of journeys like this one.</p>
    <p class="muted xsmall">Drawn in context on <a href="/spiral/">The Spiral</a>.</p>
